  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>From the given&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>140</mn></math>&nbsp;students, all even numbered students opted Mathematics&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mi>M</mi></mfenced><mo>,</mo></math>&nbsp;hence, the number of students opted Mathematics is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>M</mi><mo>&#8801;</mo><mfenced open=\"[\" close=\"]\" separators=\"|\"><mfrac><mn>140</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>70</mn><mo>,</mo></math>&nbsp;where&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced open=\"[\" close=\"]\"><mi>x</mi></mfenced></math>&nbsp;denotes the greatest integer function of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>.</mo></math></p><p>Similarly, the students who opted Physics are&nbsp;<math><mi>P</mi><mo>&#8801;</mo><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\" separators=\"|\"><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mn>140</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>46</mn></math></p><p>And, the&nbsp;students who opted Chemistry are&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>C</mi><mo>&#8801;</mo><mfenced open=\"[\" close=\"]\" separators=\"|\"><mfrac><mn>140</mn><mn>5</mn></mfrac></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>28</mn></math></p><p>Similarly, the students who opted Mathematics and&nbsp;Physics are the numbers which are divisible by both&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#38;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>3</mn></math>&nbsp;i.e.&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>6</mn><mo>,</mo></math>&nbsp;and their number is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced open=\"[\" close=\"]\" separators=\"|\"><mfrac><mn>140</mn><mn>6</mn></mfrac></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>23</mn></math></p><p>The students who opted Mathematics and&nbsp;Chemistry are the numbers which are divisible by both&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#38;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>5</mn></math>&nbsp;i.e.&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>10</mn><mo>,</mo></math>&nbsp;and their number is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced open=\"[\" close=\"]\" separators=\"|\"><mfrac><mn>140</mn><mn>10</mn></mfrac></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>14</mn></math></p><p>The students who opted Physics and&nbsp;Chemistry are the numbers which are divisible by both&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#38;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>5</mn></math>&nbsp;i.e.&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>15</mn><mo>,</mo></math>&nbsp;and their number is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced open=\"[\" close=\"]\"><mfrac><mn>140</mn><mn>15</mn></mfrac></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>9</mn></math></p><p>And, the students who opted all the three subjects are the numbers which are divisible by&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#38;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>5</mn></math>&nbsp;i.e.&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>30</mn><mo>,</mo></math>&nbsp;and their number is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced open=\"[\" close=\"]\"><mfrac><mn>140</mn><mn>30</mn></mfrac></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn></math><br /><br /><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/lgybaoxnglxtplxvwyxihtoncujjkwcdjxetzmsintfnfdzvgs.png\" /></p><p>Now, using<br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>n</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>&#8746;</mo><mi>C</mi><mo>&#8746;</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mi>n</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mi>P</mi></mfenced><mo>+</mo><mi>n</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mi>C</mi></mfenced><mo>+</mo><mi>n</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mi>M</mi></mfenced><mo>-</mo><mi>n</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>&#8745;</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>-</mo><mi>n</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>&#8745;</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>-</mo><mi>n</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>&#8745;</mo><mi>P</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>+</mo><mi>n</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>&#8745;</mo><mi>M</mi><mo>&#8745;</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>46</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>28</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>70</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>9</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>14</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>23</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn></math></p><p><math><mo>=</mo><mn>102</mn></math></p><p>Thus,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>102</mn></math>&nbsp;students have opted for atleast one of the three subjects.</p><p>Hence, number of students who did not opt for any of the three courses <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>140</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>102</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>38</mn><mo>.</mo></math></p>",
